------------------------------------------------------------
ARCHITECTURE (mirrors the landed BatteryRadialGauge precedent)
------------------------------------------------------------
- The View + model take an injected `Shared.AutomationsStore` (KMP S8 holder, ADR-004) and
  compile against the staged Shared.xcframework. No HTTP / query-key logic in the view.
- Data sources bound through the @Observable model (web hook names preserved at call sites):
    useAutomations          -> store.automations() : StateFlow<Resource<List<Automation>>>
                               -> StateHolderModel -> LoadableState<[Automation]> -> [AutomationRow]
    useBulkAutomationsUpdate -> store.bulkAutomationsUpdate(ids:op:) (async throws)
- KMP interop pinned against the generated Shared.h header (verified, not assumed):
    AutomationsStore.automations()                          swift_name("automations()")
    AutomationsStore.bulkAutomationsUpdate(ids:op:)          async (completionHandler bridge)
    AutomationBulkOp.enable / .disable / .delete_           (delete -> delete_, ObjC keyword)
    Automation.id / .name / .description_ / .enabled / .executionCount   (description_ = NSObject clash)
    KotlinLong(longLong:)                                   for NSArray<SharedLong *>
- All display/selection logic lives in pure, KMP-free value types so it is unit-tested without
  the live graph (same strategy as the dashboard widgets): AutomationRow projection,
  BulkSelection (web useBulkSelection), AutomationListPhase.resolve, AutomationBulkOperation.
- SI: this surface carries no unit-bearing fields (the Automations domain is unit-free), so no
  conversion is required; formatting stays at the render boundary per P1/S5.
- Live SSE: GET /automations is a polled query (no SSE source), so no live subscription /
  staleness indicator is required for this page (4 data states only: loading/empty/error/success).

